course: dictionary
lesson: 1876
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word collar can name a thing you wear, a thing round an animal's neck, or a ring round something. It can also be an action: to collar someone means to catch and hold them. The sentence tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Cats are hunters by instinct; bringing prey home may be sharing or showing off, and a bell on the collar can warn birds and mice.» Here a collar is a band round a cat's neck, because a cat can wear a bell on it. Ask yourself: what could be on a neck? That clue points to the right meaning.
explain: Look at the words around the hard word. Is it a thing, or something someone does? A collar on a shirt is a thing you can touch. To collar a person is an action, something you do, so it is a verb.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A collar can be a part of a shirt, coat or dress that goes round the neck.
fact: A collar can be a band of leather or another material round an animal's neck, such as a dog's collar.
fact: A collar can also be any ring or band round something, such as a metal collar round a pipe.
fact: To collar someone means to catch and hold them, or to stop them to talk to them.
exercise: «Cats are hunters by instinct; a bell on the collar can warn birds and mice.» What is the collar in this sentence? | A part of a shirt that goes round the neck | To catch and hold someone | *A band round a cat's neck | A metal ring round a pipe
exercise: Ellie's teacher says, «Pull your collar straight before assembly.» What is a collar here? | A way to stop someone and talk to them | A ring round a pipe | A band round an animal's neck | *The part of a shirt that goes round the neck
exercise: «Officer Reid had to collar the thief before he ran off.» What does collar mean? | *To catch and hold someone | A band round a neck | A metal ring round a pipe | Part of a shirt
test: «Releasing is very hard: an animal born in a zoo ... then wears a radio collar so scientists can see if it survives.» What is a radio collar? | A radio that plays music in the wild | A metal ring round a radio | *A band round an animal's neck that carries a radio | A collar on a shirt for a radio presenter
test: In the phrase «turn up your collar», what is a collar? | To catch and hold someone | A ring round a pipe | A band round a dog's neck | *The part of a coat that goes round the neck
exam: Tom says collar only means a dog's band. Which answer is correct? | *Collar has several meanings: a shirt part, an animal's band, a ring round something, and a verb meaning to catch someone | Collar means only a dog's band, so Tom is right | Collar only means to talk to someone | Collar is a colour
